{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "3b6ea7bc-9731-836b-bdab-83714dd74e0c",
  "created_at": "2026-02-02T11:26:33-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Andres Salazar",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:24:26-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:24:28-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, hi. Um, can you hear me okay? I'm in my car, well, parked, but the signal is kind of bad over here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:24:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. What can I help you with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:24:40-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I just got a letter, or a flyer, I don't know, it was taped to the bin actually, and my neighbor was telling me the rules changed on recycling. She was telling me this whole thing about her cousin's town in Massachusetts, which, anyway. [line breaks up] so what can go in now? Like pizza boxes. Are those okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:24:58-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Pizza boxes, generally if they're clean they're fine, but if they're soaked in grease, that part goes in the trash. Tearing off the dirty part works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:06-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay, so half and half. What about glass? Because I thought glass was a different thing, like a separate drop-off, or was that the old way?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:15-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bottles and jars can go in the bin, rinsed out. Let me jot this down as we go."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, and the clamshells, the plastic ones from, like, berries and salad. I always see the little triangle with a number and I never know. [inaudible] sorry, what?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:30-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said the clamshells depend on the number on the bottom, so check the flyer on the bin. If you tell me yours, I can look it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:39-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, it's, hold on, I don't have the flyer in the car. Okay, forget that, I'll look at home. Oh, and the bin itself, the lid cracked, the whole hinge thing is broken. How do I ask for a replacement?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:51-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can put in a request for you. Do you have something to write with? I'll give you the details."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:25:58-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, yeah, I've got a pen ready and a scrap of paper, the back of a receipt. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:04-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "First I need the location for the replacement."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh right, sorry. It's 48 Farewell Street, in the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:11-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 48 Farewell. Request is in for a replacement bin. Is the recycling one or the trash one that's broken?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:18-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Uh, the recycling. The blue one. Wait, is the lid supposed to be blue? Mine's kind of faded."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:24-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Faded blue is fine, that's the one. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-02T11:26:27-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think that's it. I'm still not sure about the clamshells, but I'll check the number. Thanks."
    }
  ],
